It replaces every element in the range [beg, end] that matches old_val with new_val according to the predicatate (passed callable) condition.

```cpp
replace_copy(beg, end, dest, old_val, new_val);
```

The same as replace but copies the result of the operation to the destination itrator (dest) and leaves the values in the range denoted by [beg, end] intact.

